{
  "notes": "Lo-fi, F major, 82 BPM, swung sixteenths (58.5 %). A Rhodes (with its tremolo) comping rootless four-note voicings, an upright bass on roots and fifths, the player's dusty piano on the Smart Keys (LOFI KEYS: an old upright with tape wow), the LO-FI kit, and the record on the master: DUST crackle and bit loss, slow chorus wobble, a dark room, a little ducking. Scenes: A the Rhodes alone on IVmaj7 Imaj7; B IVmaj7 Imaj7 vi7 ii7 (every ninth diatonic, so the rootless voicings stay sweet); C a ii V I vi turnaround with busier drums; D IVmaj7 ii7, almost empty. ENERGY never changes the swing: it adds the bass, then kick, snare and eighth hats, then ghost sixteenths, the shaker and fills; the levels give a little back at the top. All material is original.",
